      "writtenOn": "2026-06-15T21:02:04Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I don\u0027t think this code needs to be project specific.  This could be moved into the PDC subsystem.  The parameter JAINA_MAX_DISCHARGING_CURRENT_MA and  JAINA_MAX_DISCHARGING_POWER_MW could be added to the the existing [`usbc-port-policy`](https://source.chromium.org/chromiumos/chromiumos/codesearch/+/HEAD:src/platform/ec/zephyr/dts/bindings/usbc/usbc-port-policy.yaml;l\u003d11).\n\nDefault values of 0 would bypass the throttle logic.  This can be done by creating a Kconfig that depends on the property getting set:\n\n```\nMAX_DISCHARGE_CURRENT_PROP :\u003d max_dicharge_current_ma\nMAX_DISCHARGE_POWER_PROP :\u003d max_dicharge_power_mw\n\nconfig PDC_POWER_MGMT_SRC_THROTTLING\n\tbool \"Enable SRC throttling\"\n\tdefault y\n\tdepends on $(dt_compat_any_has_prop,$(DT_COMPAT_USBC_PORT_POLICY),$(MAX_DISCHARGE_CURRENT_PROP)) || \\\n\t\t$(dt_compat_any_has_prop,$(DT_COMPAT_USBC_PORT_POLICY),$(MAX_DISCHARGE_POWER_PROP))\n```",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 78,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 78,
        "endChar": 48
      },
      "revId": "b31a396ba3ed175f6bb50f4fe89930420e0b67cd",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
